WEBVTT

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.620
Well? How does it feel?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.330
Don't care.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.830
The information you provided
on Mondenkind has come in handy.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:24.700
So I passed the test? Well, I have
worked there longer than your spy.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.870
That aside, how is Hiems coming along?

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.910
We're finishing up with his camouflage.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.500
But there is no guarantee that you can
pilot him once he's ready to go.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:39.120
You're worried about that
at this point in the game?

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:41.120
Don't get full of yourself.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:45.910
iDOLs will never follow our bidding.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.250
Redacted

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.580
Affiliation:

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.950
Imber...

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.410
Kono sora no shita itsu made mo
Underneath this sky, I have always

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.830
Sagashi tsuzuketa yume
Continued to search for my dream

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:35.370
Hitorikiri...
All alone...

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:41.040
Doko e minna tabidatsu no?
Where does everyone go forth for their journey?

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.580
Kioku no hibi ga toozakaru
The days in my memories grow distant

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:51.290
Ano koro no egao wa
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:58.080
Mune no naka ima wo sasaeteta
Your smile from back then supports my heart now

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:08.370
Mugon no yokogao de anata mo watashi mo kitto
I'm sure that with our silent profiles, both you and I

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.950
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo
Understood that these personas exist

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.540
Kizu yue no persona wakatte ita yo
Because of our injuries

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:19.200
Shiawase no tame ni ai no tame dakara to
We say we do this for happiness or for love

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.620
Zankoku na tatakai wo kuri kaeshite
As we repeat this cruel battle

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.290
Sore de mo namida ga tomaranai
Yet even so, the tears won't stop

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.660
Negau kokoro wa issho
Our hopeful hearts are one

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:38.450
Sorezore no mirai ga yobunda
Our own futures are calling to us

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:45.910
iDOL and Idol

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:54.410
In the end, we couldn't find
any indication of what caused this.

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.580
Right.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:03:00.330
We spent the past week poring over
everything we could get our hands on,

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:01.410
but to no avail.

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:04.410
He was wiped totally clean of the incident.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:09.700
But while we were at it, we managed
to confirm that he isn't bugged.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.290
Isn't that a good thing?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:14.830
Indeed. About how much longer before
we can put him back on missions?

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.700
Right. We're just about done
updating his cockpit,

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:24.200
but we still need to scan all of his
control programs to play it safe.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.500
Between conducting checks
and reinstalling programs,

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:27.620
it'll take another week...

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:28.450
I see...

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:33.910
Isn't the timing perfect? Iori has fully
recovered and Amami could use the break.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.660
Yes, you're right.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:43.370
Ma'am?

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.000
You're still here? Didn't you hear
that you're on leave?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.870
Uh, yeah, I received word, but...

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.700
But?

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.120
Are you all that worried
about Chihaya Kisaragi?

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.950
There were your viewing records
in the reference room.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:04.580
Wasn't she Imber's very first Master?

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.040
That's right.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:11.620
Why did she leave Imber?
Did she abandon Imber when she left?

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.580
iDOL Roasted
Sweet Potatoes

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:16.080
Actually, if I had to say, it's the opposite.

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:22.040
I've told you about the Dawn of
the Purple Moon once before, haven't I?

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:28.750
Didn't people with information prior to
the incident protect Imber and Nebula...?

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:29.790
You're wrong.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:37.120
Imber was the one she wanted to take
with her the most, but Imber rejected her.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.330
Until then, he had never rejected her
so much as once.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:45.790
And after that, Imber went
into a deep sleep.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:48.700
He refused any form
of contact from anyone.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.540
Clear up until you showed up.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:57.200
What was Imber thinking?
Or was that merely an accident?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.950
No one knows the truth. No one.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.910
Imber rejected his Master...?

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.910
Café
Monsieur

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.000
Grow to dislike someone?

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:11.790
Uh, right. For instance, Yayoi, haven't
the two of us always been friends?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:17.750
So I was wondering what it would take
for you to suddenly hate me one day.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:20.660
Grow to hate you...?

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.750
I know! It's about that boy
from your club, isn't it?

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:27.620
What's up? Did you get in a fight?

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:33.410
Er, it's not like that. It-it's just,
the last time I was on him-

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:34.450
On him?

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.370
When did you go that far?!

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:40.700
No, I didn't mean it like that!
When I went inside of him-

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:43.620
You went IN him?! Don't tell me you-

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.370
I didn't! So, um, at school! Right!

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.290
At school, there was a picture
inside of his desk.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:51.660
A picture?

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.410
Uh, yeah...

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:58.120
It was a picture of a girl
he used to know a while back.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.330
Oh, uh-huh!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.250
He used to get along
really well with that girl,

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.870
but then one day he suddenly...

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.410
Ah-hah! I get it!

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:11.870
So you're nervous that
you'll meet the same fate, right?

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:15.040
Is that it?

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:19.790
If that's the problem,
leave everything to me!

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:23.660
Aren't you off for the day?

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.910
Girls Santa
Contest 07

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:30.910
Girls Santa
Contest 07

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.790
It-it's short!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.540
How is it? Oh, don't you look adorable?

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:44.250
I-I can't do this after all! I can't go out
in front of people like this!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:46.540
Actually, it's going to be broadcast on TV.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:53.040
Girls Santa
Contest Entries

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.830
I can't! I can't! I can't! I have
a pimple here and a mole here!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.830
Plus I've gained some weight!
There is NO WAY I'm going on TV!

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:58.620
You'll be fine, just fine!
The camera won't pick that stuff up.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:06:59.410
But...!

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:03.830
You'll be the star of your class if you
tell them you entered a contest on TV!

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:08.580
There's no way that boy would want
to break up with a girl like that.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.700
Huh? Y-you think so?

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:13.620
At least, that's what a manga
I just read said.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.910
Yayoi...

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.950
C'mon! It's about to start!

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:18.620
Wait!

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:26.120
Ami
Futami

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.120
The nightshift sure is tough...

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:29.330
It's the "Girls Santa Contest"!

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.330
Miss Santa Entry No. 8, you're up!

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:35.040
Uh, I'm Haruka Amami.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:37.370
Um, my friend asked me to come...

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:38.200
Wh... Why?
Um, my friend asked me to come...

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.830
Why on Earth were you on TV?!

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:45.290
L-like I said, Yayoi made me.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:46.910
You should have turned her down!

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:50.080
I see. This was broadcast
nationwide yesterday.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.500
Anyway, this goes against the rules!
Sir, isn't that right?

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.290
Why not let her do as she wishes?

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:02.660
What?!

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:05.700
True, it is fundamentally against office rules

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:09.790
for anyone on the iDOL Team
to tell outsiders about our organization.

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.160
But as long as you keep it a secret,

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:16.160
you are free to do as you wish
when you are off work.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.870
Actually, I've done so myself...

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.750
JOSEPH SHINGETSU'S
VETERAN AT THE
TEA CEREMONY
THE HEART OF THE TEA
RESIDES IN A
WELL-TRAINED BODY...!!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.700
See, the scribbles
I wrote while hospitalized

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:25.450
attracted the attention of
a major publisher!

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:28.700
If you're interested,
would you two like a copy?

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.910
In other words, someone
broke in from the outside,

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.750
swapped out the maintenance Eye
and fled without anyone ever noticing.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.450
Correct?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.790
You've been part of
the iDOL Team the longest,

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:48.250
so don't tell me that you actually believe
that report, Azusa Miura.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.250
Let's face reality here!

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:57.080
Wasn't data for the hangar's
surveillance camera wiped clean?

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.540
But not until after the incident.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.660
Only someone on the inside could pull off...
a stunt like that.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:06.580
An inside job?

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:09.870
It's highly likely that it was someone
who can move around the base freely

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:12.080
without arousing suspicion.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:13.870
For instance...

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.330
It could be you.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:23.080
"You make it look as
if you hate them the most,

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.620
"but are actually secretly communicating
with your sister in Turiavita."

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.040
It's a common story.

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.000
Are you serious?

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.290
Of course...

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.250
...I was joking.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.450
The program is running like normal.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.750
I've completed checking items
up to 40 on the chart.

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:41.830
Where did I put the guide
for the inner-shell controller?

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:44.790
Sweet! We're done checking
the items on the activation list!

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:48.620
Well, Ribbon? How does
your new seat feel?

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.910
Seems okay.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.540
Great! Could you wait there a minute?

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:02.410
You'll be the star of your class if you tell
them you entered a contest on TV!

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:06.750
There's no way that boy would want
to break up with a girl like that.

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:09.790
Or something.

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.950
Isn't this... a game? But why?

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.870
Oh, that? I uploaded it for our tutorial test.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:26.500
It turned on by itself?
Crap, is there another bug?

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:29.080
Okay, I'll run another check.

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:33.450
But Imber might be saying
he wants to play with you, Ribbon.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:50.660
In that case, take that!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:54.700
Then how about...

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:06.120
Oh, good morning.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.540
Wh-what's the matter, Yayoi?

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.290
At last! It's finally happened!

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:14.290
What has?

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:15.290
Haruka!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.000
Ouch!

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:20.540
A scout! A SCOUT!

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:22.040
Come again?

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:24.750
My agency's president saw
that show the other day

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.910
and asked if you're interested in show biz!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.620
He's interested in who?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.410
You, Haruka! Of course you're
interested, aren't you?

00:11:31.410 --> 00:11:34.700
After all, you came to Tokyo
to become an idol!

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:36.160
Uh...

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.790
Okay, that settles it!

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.660
Anyway, come by my agency!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.540
Thus begins the legend of the idols
Haruka and Yayoi!

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.750
Uh, ummm... Yayoi?

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.540
Hurry up and get dressed!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.200
Yayoi, give me a sec!

00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.290
Look! It's about to start.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:00.870
Good evening!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:01.700
Iori?
Good evening!

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.410
I know, I know! Sheesh,
why is it always her?
Tonight we have another episode
of "Yayoi-style Radio"!

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:06.250
I know, I know! Sheesh,
why is it always her?
I'm your host, Yayoi Takatsuki!

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:07.120
How is everyone spending their autumn nights?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.620
Hey, it's starting!
How is everyone spending their autumn nights?

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.870
Wait! Wait!
How is everyone spending their autumn nights?

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:10.080
Hurry up!
How is everyone spending their autumn nights?

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:10.750
Hurry up!
Well, tonight we have a special guest here with us!

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.500
Well, tonight we have a special guest here with us!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.500
Fresh from her debut,

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:16.910
this is a sparkling newborn idol!

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:18.870
Naturally, this is her first appearance
on the show!

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.250
It's Haruka Amami!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.330
M-move your mouth...

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.910
Right! Th-thanks for having me!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.700
Ouch!

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:36.250
S-so then, let's start off with a self-introduction.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:36.750
When is your birthday?

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:41.250
Uh, I wasn't interested in doing this, but my friend-

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:42.500
Haruka, say your birthday!

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:44.410
Huh? Er, April-

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.200
You're blowing into the mic! Back up!

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.330
April 3rd!

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:48.410
That's too far!

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.910
I really can't do this! I can't be an idol.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:58.700
But isn't this your first week?
Everyone's like this in the beginning.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:03.500
I can't do it! I can't talk as well as you
and I'm not as cute!

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.080
Idols don't whine.

00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.330
Boo!

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:07.790
Idols don't pout.

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.160
Idols don't whimper!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.700
Haruka, didn't you want to become one?
To be an idol?

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:19.330
Uh, yeah, but now I have school...

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:23.160
But even the prez said we'd give
your education top priority!

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.870
True, but...

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:28.330
And I'll support you the best I can. Okay?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.370
Let's stick with it a while longer.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.330
Or so Yayoi said, but really...

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.750
I'm not sure if I'm cut out for it.

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:46.540
Imber, I wouldn't get to hang out
with you as much. And then...

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:48.290
O-okay! It-it's nice to meet you!

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:50.370
Is-isn't this...?
Right! Th-thanks for having me! Ouch!

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:51.040
Right! Th-thanks for having me! Ouch!

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:52.500
When is your birthday?

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.370
Wh-why do you have a copy of that?!
When is your birthday?

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.700
I'm sure Imber is cheering for you as well.
When is your birthday?

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.700
I'm sure Imber is cheering for you as well.
Uh, I wasn't interested in doing this, but my friend-

00:13:58.700 --> 00:13:59.790
Yukiho?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:01.500
You could be absolutely right!

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.500
The same goes for that game.

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:08.830
It looks like Imber has been
interested in you for a while.

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:12.790
Imber might enjoy getting to see
the different sides of you.

00:14:12.790 --> 00:14:14.200
That's right.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:18.410
Haruka, I'm sure you're capable
of handling both jobs.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.000
We'll help you out, too.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:23.080
Well, as much as we can.

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:29.410
Okay! I'll give it a try.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:36.620
Natsu no sora ni chikatta yume
The dream I swore upon the summer sky

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:42.160
Zutto kono mune ni kagayaku kara
Will shine in my heart forever

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:47.500
Donna toki mo mayowazu yuku yo
So no matter what, I'll carry on without floundering

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:52.120
Aoi kioku ni hansha shiteku
Let's dress the future up with

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.830
Negai no broach wo
The broach of dreams

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.200
Mirai ni kazarou
That reflects my blue memories

00:14:58.200 --> 00:15:01.330
Kizuna wo shinjiteru
I believe in our bonds

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:05.950
Nee, watashi wo mitsumete
Hey, please look at me

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:05.950
What? So now she's working as an idol?

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:09.000
Uh-huh. It looks like
she's working hard at it.

00:15:09.120 --> 00:15:11.040
She has lessons and goes
around meeting people.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:13.160
She said that there is a lot for her to learn.

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:16.660
But is this okay? Really?

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:18.660
Squall mitai na tomadoi
This confusion is like a squall

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.200
Well, why not?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:21.910
Tate musubi no koi
It's a granny knot romance

00:15:19.200 --> 00:15:21.700
